<title>GERMANY: Siemens in Korean power station deal.</title>
<headline>Siemens in Korean power station deal.</headline>
<dateline>ERLANGEN, Germany 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>German electronics group Siemens AG on Friday said it signed a deal with South Korea's Korea Heavy Industries &amp; Construction (Hanjung) for it to supply Siemens' Teleperm power station control system.</p>
<p>The digitally-based Teleperm system operates with either oil, gas or coal-fired power stations.</p>
<p>The two are already working together to build eight 500 megawatt power station units in South Korea.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
